<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # Learning to Relax – Lesson # 5</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0;"><i>Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</i></p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 5</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Mediation</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Grade:</b> 12th Grade (CEFR: B1.3)</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Scenario:</b> Learning to Balance</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Theme:</b> Learning to Relax</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Mediation: Concept: Explain complex ideas with simple examples. Communication: Assist in clear communication of plans and roles.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Mediation: Can explain time management strategies with simple examples and gestures (e.g., points to a timer to indicate time management). Can assist in communication roles through miming or visuals (e.g., points to someone for "notetaker" and uses "writing" with a pencil gesture to indicate the role). Can use basic bilingual terms to bridge understanding in discussions on school-life balance (e.g., "Take a break and relax, like 'descanso,' for a few minutes to clear your mind.").</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>
<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <th style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 33%;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 33%;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333; background-color: #f2f2f2; width: 34%;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Engagement, Modeling and Clarification)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher displays two contrasting images on the board: one showing a student looking overwhelmed with a pile of books, and another showing a student calmly working at a neat desk, possibly with a plant nearby. Students work in pairs to discuss what each image represents regarding "school-life balance" and "stress." The teacher prompts them to consider how they would explain these images to someone who doesn't speak English well. (e.g., "How would you simplify 'overwhelmed'?")</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models explaining the concept of "time management" using simple language, gestures, and a bilingual term. "Time management is about organizing your schedule to use your time well, like 'organizar tu tiempo.' You need to prioritize tasks, deciding what's most important first." The teacher uses hand gestures for 'organizing' and 'prioritizing'.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b>
                <ul style="margin-bottom: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What does it mean to 'prioritize' tasks? Can you show me with a gesture?" (Checks understanding of verb 'prioritize' and non-verbal mediation.)</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If I said 'time management is like 'gestión del tiempo',' does that help you understand?" (Checks understanding of bilingual mediation.)</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___ / ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Learning to Balance")</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> The teacher presents short video clips or printed examples of infographics explaining complex ideas in a simplified way. This includes examples of effective use of visuals, minimal text, and clear explanations. One example will focus on a "mindfulness" technique or a "stress relief" activity. Genre: educational infographic examples, short instructional video excerpts. Register: informative, accessible. Format: digital and print visuals.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Students analyze how visual and textual elements work together to explain concepts simply and bridge understanding for diverse audiences, enhancing their ability to mediate information effectively.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b>
                <ul style="margin-bottom: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students identify 2-3 common strategies used in the examples to simplify complex information (e.g., using icons, short sentences, analogies).</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">True/False: "Effective infographics use long paragraphs to explain every detail." (False) "Using gestures can help explain concepts during a presentation." (True)</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___ / ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">7-10 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Accuracy focus on Mediation)</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students practice explaining time management strategies, using present perfect continuous to discuss ongoing efforts, second conditional for hypothetical improvements, and modals for suggestions (should, might, can, could). They also focus on integrating key vocabulary (balance, routine, schedule, stress, relaxation, mindfulness, time management) and differentiating /ɪ/ and /iː/ sounds.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b>
                <ul style="margin-bottom: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 1 (Controlled Practice - Concept Matching & Simplification):</b> The teacher provides a list of complex terms related to school-life balance and relaxation (e.g., 'procrastination,' 'mindfulness,' 'flexible routine,' 'restorative downtime'). Students work individually to match each term with a simpler explanation from a provided bank or write their own simple one-sentence explanation. Then, in pairs, they practice explaining these terms to each other using gestures or basic examples, focusing on clear pronunciation of /ɪ/ in 'activities' and /iː/ in 'relieve' if applicable.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 2 (Semi-controlled - Suggestion Scenarios):</b> The teacher gives pairs different scenarios (e.g., "Explain how to 'allocate time' effectively to a student who is always busy with activities," or "Suggest ways to 'unwind' after a stressful week to a friend from another country"). Students must formulate explanations and suggestions using target grammar (modals like "You might try...", "You could consider...", "I think you should...") and vocabulary, while also being prepared to use a simple gesture or a bilingual term if their partner pretends not to understand. For instance, "If I had more free time, I would try mindfulness exercises to relieve stress."</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Activity 3 (Pair Interaction - Infographic Explanation Prep):</b> Students get into their project groups for the Time Management Infographic. Each student takes a section of their infographic draft and practices explaining it to their group members as if they were explaining it to a younger student or someone unfamiliar with the topic. They receive feedback on clarity, use of simple language, and whether they successfully used gestures or could incorporate a basic bilingual term (e.g., "Take a break, like 'descanso,' for five minutes"). They practice giving suggestions to each other for improvement: "You have been explaining that well, but you might need to add a visual for 'prioritize.'"</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___ / ___</p>
                <p style="text-align="justify">15-20 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">(Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Learning to Balance")</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Group Presentation of the "Time Management Infographic." Students present their completed (or near-completed) infographics to the class. The focus is on their ability to mediate the information effectively. They will explain their chosen time management strategies (e.g., 'prioritizing tasks,' 'setting boundaries,' 'allocating downtime') to their peers, who are acting as a varied audience (some may pretend to be younger students, some non-native speakers needing clarification). This task integrates the 21st Century Skills Project, allowing students to lead collaborative projects on relaxation and school-life balance.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connect to Theme and Scenario:</b> Students must clearly explain how their infographic strategies contribute to "Learning to Balance" social life, schoolwork, and relaxation, using simple examples and effective gestures. For instance, explaining "downtime" by mimicking relaxing or pointing to a clock for "time management." They will also assist group members in communicating their parts, perhaps by using a visual aid for them or rephrasing a point. They should integrate bilingual terms where appropriate to bridge understanding (e.g., "mindfulness, like 'atención plena'"). Students will use present perfect continuous to talk about how they have been trying to balance their schedules while creating the infographic, and modals to give suggestions for others.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___ / ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative assessment strategy:</b> Teacher Observation Checklist and Peer Assessment.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Students present their Time Management Infographic, with specific attention paid to how they explain the strategies and mediate understanding.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b>
                <ul style="margin-bottom: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity of explanation: Explains complex ideas with simple language and examples.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use of non-verbal mediation: Effectively uses gestures, miming, or visuals to clarify points.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Assistance in communication: Helps group members or clarifies roles effectively.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Integration of target language: Uses present perfect continuous, second conditional, and modals for suggestions, and appropriate vocabulary.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Use of basic bilingual terms: Appropriately uses a Spanish equivalent to bridge understanding when necessary.</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Pronunciation: Distinguishes between /ɪ/ and /iː/ where appropriate (e.g., 'activities' vs 'relieve').</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b>
                <ul style="margin-bottom: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was one strategy from our infographic that I was able to explain clearly using simple examples or gestures?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How did I help my group members communicate their ideas effectively during the presentation?"</li>
                </ul></p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___ / ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-8 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student self-reflection prompt:</b>
                <ul style="margin-bottom: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How has working on this Time Management Infographic helped me understand and explain strategies for a balanced life? What 'new' ways of explaining things did I try?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What challenges did I face when trying to simplify complex ideas, and how might I overcome them in the future?"</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher reflection:</b>
                <ul style="margin-bottom: 0; padding-left: 20px;">
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What worked well in terms of students' ability to mediate information and explain their infographics?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What adjustments or scaffolds are needed for students to further develop their mediation skills, especially in using bilingual terms or more sophisticated gestures?"</li>
                    <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Were the instructions clear enough for students to understand the mediation aspect of the project?"</li>
                </ul></p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> This is Lesson 5, the final lesson of the theme. The skills developed here, especially the ability to explain, summarize, and present information clearly, will be crucial for any future collaborative projects and for understanding complex academic texts and discussions in various subjects.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="padding: 8px; border: 1px dashed #333;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">___ / ___ / ___</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">3-5 minutes</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>